  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A rectangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> with end points of the one of its sides as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is inscribed in a circle. If the equation of a diameter of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7dec6128-8e1b-46fa-8389-4c094375032c-image.png\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 167px;\" /></p><p>Equation&nbsp;of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now the given diameter is parallel to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>Then, the distance between diameter and line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Also&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>20</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Area of the rectangle<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
